This Audience Participation Exercise comes in three questions. I expect,
encourage, and ask for CALM debate, however, as we have a no-debate/no
arguing policy on the nintadni list, please restrict all debate to the main
one.

{ko'a jungau ko'e lo na'e jetnu .i ru na'e jungau ra lo jetnu .i ru bacru
noda}
"He tells them something other than the truth. He does something other than
tell them the truth. He says nothing."

1: What circumstances can be described by /only one/ of the first two
bridi? (I'd like examples both ways, please.)
2: What circumstances can be described by /both/ of the first two bridi?
3: I think the last bridi is an example answer for 2. Why am I right or
wrong?

Also, if you like this kind of APE, let me know, I'll think of others. I
imagine this will be easier than trying to think of new ways to get you to
jbociska, like the earlier set was. ;)

mu'o mi'e .aionys.

